1
00:01:38,110 --> 00:01:44,000
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,100 --> 00:01:46,890
[Episode 27]

3
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:07,640
Who is it?

4
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:11,470
P-President.

5
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:12,890
President Long.

6
00:02:13,630 --> 00:02:16,310
I heard you two are together.

7
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:17,360
-Yes.
-Yes.

8
00:02:18,870 --> 00:02:19,930
Congratulations.

9
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,400
I want to talk to Liu Zhengliang

10
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,520
alone.

11
00:02:28,310 --> 00:02:29,190
Is that okay?

12
00:02:29,910 --> 00:02:30,870
Alone, right?

13
00:02:32,030 --> 00:02:33,470
Then I... I should go out.

14
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:36,360
Okay.

15
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,000
Wait, I'll put on a mink coat.

16
00:02:38,030 --> 00:02:38,829
It's too cold.

17
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:43,430
Go ahead and talk.

18
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:43,870
Sorry.

19
00:02:43,870 --> 00:02:44,960
It's fine. No big deal.

20
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:46,490
You... wait for me a moment.

21
00:02:46,630 --> 00:02:48,490
Don't leave. Wait for me a moment.

22
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:49,960
Come in. Come in.

23
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:53,630
Have a seat.

24
00:03:06,680 --> 00:03:07,470
It's good.

25
00:03:09,310 --> 00:03:10,840
Having someone by your side

26
00:03:10,840 --> 00:03:12,170
makes me feel relieved.

27
00:03:23,310 --> 00:03:24,370
Careful, it's hot.

28
00:03:25,430 --> 00:03:26,630
Let's sit for a while.

29
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:27,590
I won't sit.

30
00:03:27,590 --> 00:03:28,430
I've been sitting all day.

31
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:29,870
It's good to stand for a while.

32
00:03:29,870 --> 00:03:31,150
I find that no matter how you change,

33
00:03:31,150 --> 00:03:33,520
you are always so awkward.

34
00:03:36,150 --> 00:03:37,150
Where were you?

35
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:40,520
Are you really leaving?

36
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:43,190
How did you guess?

37
00:03:43,470 --> 00:03:44,730
Do I even need to guess?

38
00:03:45,280 --> 00:03:47,280
Otherwise, you wouldn't have
disappeared for so long,

39
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:49,540
nor would you have
come to me at this time.

40
00:03:50,310 --> 00:03:51,120
Not bad.

41
00:03:51,590 --> 00:03:52,590
You've made progress.

42
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:53,960
Hanging out with me wasn't for nothing.

43
00:03:53,960 --> 00:03:54,910
I fall for your tricks every day,

44
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:56,400
and they're always different.

45
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,630
After being fooled for so long,

46
00:03:57,630 --> 00:03:58,630
I can also summarize

47
00:03:58,630 --> 00:03:59,630
some patterns.

48
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,720
Why do you hold such a grudge?

49
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:03,470
Tell me the truth.

50
00:04:04,630 --> 00:04:05,400
Actually, I'm not that bad,

51
00:04:05,400 --> 00:04:06,360
am I?

52
00:04:08,520 --> 00:04:09,560
Just so-so.

53
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,399
Where are you planning to go?

54
00:04:18,870 --> 00:04:20,160
I got a small RV.

55
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:21,310
I'm taking my wife

56
00:04:21,310 --> 00:04:22,800
to head south all the way

57
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:25,000
and travel around the country.

58
00:04:25,630 --> 00:04:27,630
Drive anywhere and sleep anywhere.

59
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:28,750
Free and easy,

60
00:04:29,390 --> 00:04:31,240
leisurely and carefree.

61
00:04:31,480 --> 00:04:32,270
Yes.

62
00:04:32,470 --> 00:04:33,720
You're free now,

63
00:04:33,720 --> 00:04:35,040
but what about Xiaoximen Hospital?

64
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,000
It's your say now.

65
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:37,530
It has nothing to do with me.

66
00:04:38,240 --> 00:04:39,040
I'm not the president anymore.

67
00:04:39,040 --> 00:04:40,800
How does it have nothing to do with you?

68
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,560
If it weren't for you,

69
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,040
well,

70
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:45,530
Xiaoximen Hospital would have
closed down long ago.

71
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:58,050
I've already talked it over
with the headquarters.

72
00:04:59,240 --> 00:05:00,510
Retiring at this point in time

73
00:05:00,510 --> 00:05:01,870
is also in the plan.

74
00:05:03,720 --> 00:05:05,040
My departure might be more beneficial

75
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:07,440
to the development of Xiaoximen Hospital.

76
00:05:10,920 --> 00:05:11,680
That's true.

77
00:05:12,390 --> 00:05:13,720
You're getting old.

78
00:05:13,830 --> 00:05:14,600
It's time to retire.

79
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:15,530
I'll beat you up!

80
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,660
Can't you say something nice?

81
00:05:19,600 --> 00:05:20,390
What's nice?

82
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:23,000
What do you want me to say?

83
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:26,510
You don't want me
to make a statement, do you?

84
00:05:26,510 --> 00:05:27,430
Let me tell you,

85
00:05:27,920 --> 00:05:29,040
it's absolutely impossible for me

86
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:31,000
to be tied down to Xiaoximen Hospital.

87
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:31,800
As long as there's any problem,

88
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:32,630
I'll leave immediately.

89
00:05:32,630 --> 00:05:33,600
Even if there's no problem,

90
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:34,730
you can still leave.

91
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,870
I came just to tell you this.

92
00:05:41,720 --> 00:05:43,250
Even if Xiaoximen Hospital

93
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:45,270
is doing fine,

94
00:05:45,270 --> 00:05:46,400
if you want to leave,

95
00:05:46,630 --> 00:05:48,040
you can leave anytime.

96
00:05:49,070 --> 00:05:51,400
You don't need to consider other factors.

97
00:05:54,159 --> 00:05:55,360
You came over just to tell me this?

98
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,070
Yes.

99
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,360
About what the future
of Xiaoximen Hospital

100
00:06:02,360 --> 00:06:03,560
will exactly be like,

101
00:06:04,920 --> 00:06:07,160
only time can give the answer.

102
00:06:08,680 --> 00:06:10,940
You don't need to blame yourself either.

103
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,480
What do I have to blame myself for?

104
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,140
What does it have to do with me?

105
00:06:16,390 --> 00:06:17,850
If you can think like that,

106
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,040
I'm relieved.

107
00:06:19,160 --> 00:06:19,950
I'm leaving.

108
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:23,050
President Long.

109
00:06:30,830 --> 00:06:32,090
Fasten your seatbelt.

110
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:53,420
[Hospital Admission Registration]

111
00:06:50,130 --> 00:06:53,500
♪ The melting snow and the warm wind ♪

112
00:06:53,690 --> 00:06:55,990
♪ The flowers bloom again ♪

113
00:06:55,680 --> 00:06:56,360
President.

114
00:06:56,430 --> 00:06:57,040
Well,

115
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:58,430
I came specifically to find you.

116
00:06:57,260 --> 00:07:03,140
♪ It's spring; it's a remedy ♪

117
00:06:58,430 --> 00:06:59,510
For the new department—

118
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:00,970
Comrade Huang Dongsheng.

119
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:06,430
I'll leave Xiaoximen Hospital to you.

120
00:07:04,950 --> 00:07:08,530
♪ Stop and go, travelling separately ♪

121
00:07:08,830 --> 00:07:10,990
♪ At the next intersection ♪

122
00:07:12,430 --> 00:07:14,170
♪ You and I ♪

123
00:07:13,630 --> 00:07:14,360
No, no, no!

124
00:07:14,360 --> 00:07:15,310
Long, don't leave it to me!

125
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:16,040
Really, I can't do it!

126
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:16,870
Really, really!

127
00:07:16,070 --> 00:07:18,630
♪ Travel light ♪

128
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:18,240
No, this is too tiring!

129
00:07:19,260 --> 00:07:23,870
[Hospital Admission Registration]

130
00:07:20,030 --> 00:07:26,140
♪ Put the past weighing on my back
into the moon ♪

131
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:32,600
♪ Longing makes me wake up ♪

132
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:29,830
Long!

133
00:07:30,390 --> 00:07:31,240
Long!

134
00:07:32,310 --> 00:07:33,190
Long!

135
00:07:33,460 --> 00:07:37,320
♪ To the open window♪

136
00:07:33,630 --> 00:07:34,510
Long!

137
00:07:35,120 --> 00:07:36,190
Long, wait for me!

138
00:07:36,630 --> 00:07:37,760
Where are you going?

139
00:07:38,140 --> 00:07:44,650
♪ Softly, the person in my dream
is like the moonlight ♪

140
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:39,510
Long!

141
00:07:39,870 --> 00:07:40,680
Long!

142
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:45,830
Quite the presence.

143
00:07:45,350 --> 00:07:49,510
♪ Falling on my heart softly
and taking me ♪

144
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:48,040
Huang.

145
00:07:48,040 --> 00:07:49,120
Long, wait for me!

146
00:07:49,630 --> 00:07:50,510
Where are you going?

147
00:07:49,750 --> 00:07:52,310
♪ To our old familiar place ♪

148
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:52,950
[Emergency]

149
00:07:51,310 --> 00:07:52,070
Long!

150
00:07:53,010 --> 00:07:59,380
♪ Slowly, the petals fall to the center
of the lake when I miss you ♪

151
00:07:53,190 --> 00:07:53,950
Long!

152
00:07:54,270 --> 00:07:55,920
Where are you going, Long? Long!

153
00:07:55,920 --> 00:07:57,000
Long, stop the car!

154
00:07:57,040 --> 00:07:57,870
Long!

155
00:07:58,070 --> 00:07:58,920
Long!

156
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:04,350
♪ Ripples echo through the years,
with our shadows facing each other ♪

157
00:08:03,270 --> 00:08:04,110
He's running fast.

158
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:07,480
[Xiaoximen Hospital
Affiliated with Qikang Medical]

159
00:08:04,730 --> 00:08:09,890
♪ We were together on the way we came ♪

160
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:19,480
Big Pomegranate.

161
00:08:29,510 --> 00:08:30,120
Mr. Wang.

162
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:32,880
Let me come back.

163
00:08:33,080 --> 00:08:34,210
I'll sing anything.

164
00:08:40,270 --> 00:08:41,150
I'm back.

165
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,720
Welcome home, homeowner.

166
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:57,510
Where did you get this outfit?

167
00:08:57,510 --> 00:08:58,270
How is it?

168
00:08:58,790 --> 00:09:00,240
I went for a job interview.

169
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:01,270
You applied to be a security guard?

170
00:09:01,270 --> 00:09:02,120
You bet.

171
00:09:02,670 --> 00:09:04,730
Many companies were fighting for me.

172
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:06,840
I beat a bunch of old men

173
00:09:06,910 --> 00:09:08,110
and young and middle-aged people.

174
00:09:08,110 --> 00:09:08,960
They took a fancy to me.

175
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:10,120
I'm tall and give a sense of security.

176
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:10,790
Look at me.

177
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:11,510
Wait.

178
00:09:11,510 --> 00:09:11,910
How is it?

179
00:09:11,910 --> 00:09:13,840
Why did you apply for that?

180
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,320
To earn more money

181
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:18,400
and lighten your burden.

182
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:09,480
Mingming.

183
00:10:10,720 --> 00:10:11,510
Come here.

184
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,580
Do you still remember?

185
00:10:20,320 --> 00:10:21,120
Yes, I do.

186
00:10:29,630 --> 00:10:31,030
Was I handsome back then?

187
00:10:32,550 --> 00:10:34,010
You're not bad now either.

188
00:10:37,550 --> 00:10:39,750
You look more and more like your mother.

189
00:10:39,870 --> 00:10:41,400
Look how beautiful she was.

190
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:46,520
More than 20 years have passed. So fast.

191
00:10:49,750 --> 00:10:50,550
Yes.

192
00:10:52,080 --> 00:10:53,610
I'm already in my thirties.

193
00:10:59,910 --> 00:11:01,200
I've kept this photo

194
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:02,080
since then.

195
00:11:05,080 --> 00:11:06,540
I never dared to look at it.

196
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:09,770
I was afraid when I saw it...

197
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:15,650
I'd think of your mother

198
00:11:15,750 --> 00:11:16,720
and how she left.

199
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:21,080
When I saw it, I thought of

200
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,550
when I was laid off,

201
00:11:26,550 --> 00:11:27,550
how miserable

202
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:29,030
and useless I was.

203
00:11:33,630 --> 00:11:35,090
So many years have passed.

204
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,840
Just like this photo,

205
00:11:42,630 --> 00:11:44,120
I threw myself into it

206
00:11:46,200 --> 00:11:47,400
and couldn't get out.

207
00:11:54,080 --> 00:11:54,870
I know.

208
00:12:03,550 --> 00:12:05,510
Beijing is really a magical place.

209
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:11,120
I used to be like in a dream.

210
00:12:14,120 --> 00:12:16,480
A trip to Beijing woke me up.

211
00:12:18,720 --> 00:12:19,630
I woke up.

212
00:12:26,080 --> 00:12:27,150
Don't worry.

213
00:12:30,510 --> 00:12:31,840
Our days ahead

214
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,720
will definitely get better.

215
00:13:31,510 --> 00:13:32,270
My girl,

216
00:13:34,750 --> 00:13:36,550
you've worked hard these years.

217
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:58,800
[Little Pepper Stage]

218
00:14:20,060 --> 00:14:23,100
[Xiaoximen Hospital
Affiliated with Qikang Medical]

219
00:14:23,790 --> 00:14:24,840
Is my illness serious?

220
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:25,870
How long have you noticed this?

221
00:14:25,870 --> 00:14:26,670
Over 2 months.

222
00:14:26,670 --> 00:14:28,390
Why did you wait
over 2 months to see a doctor?

223
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:29,480
Have you seen Liu?

224
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,580
He's in the break room.

225
00:14:32,470 --> 00:14:34,470
At that time, because of the pain...

226
00:14:34,720 --> 00:14:36,580
You came because of the headache?

227
00:14:37,030 --> 00:14:37,840
Liu.

228
00:14:38,270 --> 00:14:39,480
I have a tricky patient upstairs.

229
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,790
Go up and take a look for me.

230
00:14:40,790 --> 00:14:41,320
Let's go.

231
00:15:08,030 --> 00:15:09,120
Hurry, hurry!

232
00:15:09,200 --> 00:15:10,390
Please stop!

233
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:11,150
Stop!

234
00:15:12,440 --> 00:15:14,670
This is too fast! Stop!

235
00:15:17,670 --> 00:15:19,120
Come, sit.

236
00:15:19,210 --> 00:15:22,670
[Health Knowledge Promotion]

237
00:15:20,030 --> 00:15:21,120
Let me introduce you.

238
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:21,840
This

239
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:23,550
is the one I just mentioned to you,

240
00:15:22,730 --> 00:15:23,460
[Expert Medical Care,
Safeguarding Public Health]

241
00:15:23,550 --> 00:15:25,680
Liu Zhengliang, Chief Physician Liu.

242
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:27,520
Chief Physician Liu?

243
00:15:27,600 --> 00:15:28,390
Yes.

244
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:30,000
Don't let his youth fool you.

245
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,240
He is the best doctor

246
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,840
in our hospital's
Neurosurgical Department.

247
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:33,670
That's great.

248
00:15:33,870 --> 00:15:35,080
With Chief Physician Liu here,

249
00:15:35,080 --> 00:15:36,540
you're definitely saved.

250
00:15:41,670 --> 00:15:43,000
Have you experienced any mental blocks

251
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:44,270
or logical gaps?

252
00:15:44,270 --> 00:15:44,870
Yes.

253
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:48,610
When was the first time
you had a mental block?

254
00:15:49,750 --> 00:15:51,750
Tell Chief Physician Liu yourself.

255
00:15:58,080 --> 00:16:00,440
I teach math

256
00:16:00,840 --> 00:16:02,170
at a junior high school.

257
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:05,360
Last month, while I was teaching,

258
00:16:05,670 --> 00:16:06,670
I suddenly couldn't remember

259
00:16:06,670 --> 00:16:08,150
a very basic formula.

260
00:16:09,670 --> 00:16:11,600
I was standing on the podium at the time,

261
00:16:11,600 --> 00:16:13,120
facing my students.

262
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:15,840
I couldn't say a single word.

263
00:16:16,270 --> 00:16:18,930
I was so anxious
that my hands and feet went cold.

264
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:21,320
I didn't know what was wrong with me.

265
00:16:22,960 --> 00:16:23,910
Go on.

266
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,600
Tell Chief Physician Liu again

267
00:16:25,600 --> 00:16:27,120
what you just told me.

268
00:16:28,960 --> 00:16:29,910
Another time,

269
00:16:30,240 --> 00:16:31,640
a student made a mistake.

270
00:16:32,030 --> 00:16:33,760
I wanted to talk to his parents.

271
00:16:34,750 --> 00:16:35,790
Suddenly,

272
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:37,840
I didn't know what to say.

273
00:16:38,270 --> 00:16:39,030
It was like,

274
00:16:40,270 --> 00:16:41,360
in my heart,

275
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,760
I knew what I wanted to do.

276
00:16:43,120 --> 00:16:43,870
And in my head,

277
00:16:43,870 --> 00:16:44,930
there were images.

278
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,410
But I just couldn't say it out loud.

279
00:16:48,670 --> 00:16:50,200
How often does this happen?

280
00:16:50,360 --> 00:16:53,870
About once a month on average.

281
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:55,870
But I feel like

282
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:58,270
the frequency is increasing.

283
00:16:59,840 --> 00:17:01,150
This is a typical manifestation

284
00:17:01,150 --> 00:17:02,600
of a tumor compressing

285
00:17:02,600 --> 00:17:04,920
language-associated functional areas.

286
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:05,720
Chief Physician Liu,

287
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:06,780
it's a brain tumor?

288
00:17:07,550 --> 00:17:08,680
What should we do?

289
00:17:10,640 --> 00:17:12,109
Don't be too nervous.

290
